        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "745f3bad-0063-5c9e-989a-2f46fe830700",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Dynasties: Nerva–Antonine dynasty\n- People: Nerva, Trajan, Hadrian, Antoninus Pius, Lucius Verus, Marcus Aurelius, Commodus\n- Roles: Roman emperors, co-emperor of Rome\n- Places: Roman Empire, Rome\n- Monuments: Great Antonine Altar\n\nFacts:\n- The Nerva–Antonine dynasty was a dynasty of seven Roman emperors who ruled the Roman Empire from 96 AD to 192 AD.\n- The emperors of the Nerva–Antonine dynasty were Nerva, Trajan, Hadrian, Antoninus Pius, Lucius Verus, Marcus Aurelius, and Commodus.\n- Lucius Verus was born on 15 December 130.\n- Lucius Verus was co-emperor of Rome with his adoptive brother Marcus Aurelius from 161 until Lucius Verus died in 169.\n- On the Great Antonine Altar, Lucius Verus stands to the right of Antoninus Pius.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5fee7557-6658-51d1-9fda-159e5d27bf55",
        "text": "Page: Nerva–Antonine dynasty. Sentence: The Nerva–Antonine dynasty was a dynasty of seven Roman Emperors who ruled over the Roman Empire from 96 AD to 192 AD.\nPage: Nerva–Antonine dynasty. Sentence: These Emperors are Nerva, Trajan, Hadrian, Antoninus Pius, Lucius Verus, Marcus Aurelius, and Commodus.\nPage: Lucius Verus. Sentence: Lucius Verus (Latin: \"Lucius Aurelius Verus Augustus\" ; 15 December 130 – 169) was the co-emperor of Rome with his adoptive brother Marcus Aurelius from 161 until his own death in 169.\nPage: Great Antonine Altar. Sentence: To the right of Antoninus Pius stands Lucius Verus.",
